+---
+name: run-local
+description: Start the 2048 app on this machine (Spring Boot API on port 8080, Vite dev server on port 5173) and smoke-test it with curl. Use when asked to run or start the app, to try a change in the browser, or to check that the API answers.
+---
+
+# Run the app locally
+
+Both servers run until they are stopped. Start each one as a background process, never as a
+blocking command.
+
+1. API: `./gradlew :api:bootRun` serves http://localhost:8080.
+2. Web: `cd web && npm run dev` serves http://localhost:5173 and proxies `/api` to the API
+   (run `npm ci` first if `web/node_modules` is missing).
+
+The web port is strict: if 5173 is taken, Vite exits instead of moving to 5174. Free the
+port; do not change `web/vite.config.ts`.
+
+## Smoke test
+
+```bash
+curl -s -X POST http://localhost:5173/api/v1/games
+```
+
+Expected: HTTP 201 and `{"data":{"id":"...","grid":[...],"score":0,"status":"IN_PROGRESS"}}`
+with exactly two non-zero tiles in `grid`. The call goes through the Vite proxy, so it
+proves both servers. Games live in memory only: restarting the API loses them.
+
+Then report the two URLs and the smoke-test result, and stop both servers when the task is
+done unless the user asked to keep them running.
